# phrase macros for question prompts: %name% expands to a random member at
# render time, so the same skill is asked many different ways and you have to
# think about what is wanted, not pattern-match the wording. every member of a
# group must be grammatically interchangeable wherever the macro is used.
#
# format:  %name% = one | two | three
#
# keep them boringly interchangeable. cleverness that only fits one sentence
# belongs inline as {a|b|c} in that one question, not here.

# --- output a thing to the screen ---
show = print | show | display | output | write out

# --- enumerate directory-ish contents ---
list = list | show | print out

# --- locate something ---
find = find | locate | hunt down | track down

# --- produce a count ---
count = count | tally | report the number of

# --- create ---
make = make | create

# --- polite framings that can prefix an instruction ---
give = give me | show me | get me | i want

# --- softeners / openers (optional flavor) ---
now = | right now | here | for me
